Web source: web/src/components/ui/DataTableColumnsMenu.tsx (THE specification).
Web-parity logic (unit-tested):
  • toggle(key): hide a visible column; refuse hiding the LAST visible one
    (web `visibleKeys.length <= 1`); show a hidden column PRESERVING original
    column order (web `order.filter(k => visibleSet.has(k) || k === key)`).
  • showAll(): every column key in column order (web `columns.map(c => c.key)`).
  • disabled = `col.required || (checked && visibleKeys.length <= 1)`
    (surfaced as a typed reason for styling + VoiceOver).
  • label = `col.header || col.key`.
i18n keys preserved VERBATIM from the web source (resolve through the P1/S10 facade):
  table.columns.menu | table.columns.button | table.columns.heading | table.columns.showAll
States reproduced (no hidden surface): loading · empty · error(retry) · loaded(menu)
  + orthogonal connectivity axis live/stale/offline (P4 leaf contract).
Telemetry: view.opened surface="DataTableColumnsMenu" (P1/S11).
A11y: trigger label "Show or hide columns, N of M visible"; per-row value
  (visible/hidden) + hint (toggle/required/last-visible); header trait on heading.

Two real defects were found+fixed in this surface that the predecessor BLOCKED run
(commit 5054ad7eb, ran on a no-Xcode runner) could not have caught because it never
compiled under Swift 6 strict concurrency:
  (1) Previews `static let actions` (non-Sendable ColumnsMenuActions) => pinned @MainActor.
  (2) The explanatory comment above it tripped swiftformat `docComments` => made it `///`.

